Per-button label overrides

Melo-Controller draws fixed Nintendo-style SF Symbols (A on the right,
L/R/ZL/ZR, minus/plus) and its layout editor names the face buttons by
their ids. An app that offers other label styles (Xbox, PlayStation)
needs to replace a button's symbol and editor name without changing the
button ids, which the saved layouts are keyed by.

New public VirtualControllerButton.iconOverrides and nameOverrides
(button id -> SF Symbol / editor name), read by ButtonView and the
layout editor's LayoutEditorNaming. The trigger and shoulder background
symbol is derived from whatever label precedes the first dot of the
icon name ("lb.rectangle.roundedbottom.fill" ->
"button.roundedbottom.horizontal.fill"), not only from "l"/"r"/"zl"/
"zr"; Melo's own symbols map exactly as before.

Upstream: not submitted.

